  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">5. Waste collected as a share of waste generated in South Tarawa where half the population lives increases.</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2021-06-14" value="44 percent (2021)" year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-06-14"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="1900-01-01"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Household waste collection increased from 3800 t/yr in 2021 to 6800 t/yr in 2024. Two of three landfills in South Tarawa are now over capacity. Funding is needed to support new landfill construction in Tarawa. Capping landfill produces usable, high land as seen in the recent rehabilitation of Betio landfill (Leney and Langley, 2024). 
Cabinet is yet to approve implementing regulations of the Environment Act 2021, including on solid waste management. With World Bank TA as part of the preparation of the second DPO in the series, these regulations are planned to be finalized in the first half of 2025. Priority regulations on the Environment and Ozone-Depleting Substances are being considered by the Office of the Attorney General, and are expected to be approved by the new Cabinet in 2024. Regulations on Protected Areas, Protected Species, Biosafety, and Recreational Reserves have been drafted and are expected to be approved in 2025-Q1.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="70 percent"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2. Government income tax revenues are increased.</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2021-06-14" value="8.7 percent of GDP (2021)" year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-06-14"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="1900-01-01"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The baseline for the RI was revised from 8.7 to 6.8 percent of GDP due to the rebasing of GDP in November 2023 with IMF assistance. The 2023 Income Tax Act came into effect in January 2024 and the accompanying regulations were approved by the Cabinet in May 2024. The audited accounts for 2025, the first full year of implementation, will be available in June 2026. The VAT Act amendment is under consultation and is expected to be submitted to Parliament between Dec 2024 and April 2025. Implementing regulations of the VAT Amendment and an updated Excise Tax Order are both expected in 2025-Q1.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="6.9 percent of GDP"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">3. PUB&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122;s average annual overdraft is reduced.</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2021-06-14" value="A$375k (2021)" year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-06-14"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="1900-01-01"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">SOE reporting practices continue to improve, with all SOEs submitting financial reports to SOEMAU in 2023. PUB&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122;s financial stability has improved as a result of better collection of receivables (including by installing prepaid meters for electricity) and the fixed price agreement for diesel with KOIL. Accounting practices improved which allow timely and accurate information on financial performance split between two key businesses of water and sanitation, and electricity supply. PUB&apos;s overdraft facility with ANZ Bank has been removed. PUB has not operated on negative balance in the last year. However, concerns remain about the financial sustainability of its water and sanitation businesses.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="A$ 0"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">4. Number of individual account holders with deposit-taking institutions is increased.</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2021-06-14" value="About 17,000 (2021)" year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-06-14"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="1900-01-01"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Financial Supervisory Authority (FSA) has been established and a locally-recruited CEO and Deputy CEO are now in place. When staffing is complete the FSA will start drafting regulations with the help of PFTAC. The number of individual accunts with ANZ Bank has increased to 22,500.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="22,500"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
